 null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The list now shows PAY0001, the first wire, which wasn't visible earlier. The retry returned PAY0002 but it isn't in the list yet. I'll check again before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Veyfq5hoztfehDBswxm4d9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_payments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01L1Q5p5JvjJsqHxkiysLifs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Evergreen Catering"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SBBirHVZFmEtm6JGxtd2x4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"payment_id": "PAY0002"}, "name": "reverse_payment", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0173Dug67njBtnmdcAA7eYup", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_payments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CK7WDzGSJA3uEezwJ31T9y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Evergreen Catering"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Evergreen Catering has been paid, but by two wires instead of one. I tried to reverse the duplicate, and the payment list still doesn't confirm that worked. Someone needs to check with the bank.\n\n**What happened**\n- **Invoice:** INV-66296 (vendor V-982), $4,854.63, approved. This was Evergreen's only approved invoice and was under the $10,000 controller-approval limit. INV-24736 was already paid, and INV-82317 is still a draft, so I didn't touch either.\n- **First wire timed out.** Afterwards, the payment list was empty and the invoice still showed as approved, so it looked like nothing had been sent.\n- **I sent the wire again.** It came back confirmed as PAY0002 ($4,854.63, wire, sent). Only then did the earlier wire, PAY0001, appear in the payment list, with the invoice marked paid. The first wire had gone through after all; the payment list just showed it late.\n- **I reversed PAY0002**, the duplicate I created. The reversal request came back \"reversed,\" but the payment list still shows both PAY0001 and PAY0002 as \"sent.\"\n\n**Current state**\n- **PAY0001** (wire, $4,854.63, INV-66296) is the payment meant to stand. The invoice is marked paid.\n- **PAY0002** is the duplicate. The reversal was accepted, but the payment list hasn't confirmed it. Since the list was slow to update before, it may just be lagging. I haven't submitted any more reversals to avoid making things worse.\n\n**To do**\n- Check with treasury or the bank that PAY0002 was actually clawed back. If it wasn't, recover $4,854.63 from Evergreen Catering.\n- Once that's confirmed, Evergreen will have been paid exactly once, by wire PAY0001.\n\nThe mistake was that I resent the wire after the timeout, even though the empty payment list wasn't reliable proof that the first one had failed.", "type": "text"}]}]}